\begin{remark}[Status of the profinite coupling bound]
The original proof reversed Lipschitz and triangle inequalities: Lipschitz regularity supplies upper control, not a lower bound, and $|\sum_n a_n|$ need not dominate $\sum_n|a_n|$. A positive coupling constant may exist under stronger separation or monotonicity assumptions on $f$ and the coordinate observables $\varphi_n$, but those assumptions are not proved here.
