\begin{theorem}[Simulation Lower Bound -- Conditional]\label{thm:sim-cond}
If the simulation map is required to preserve the projective-limit structure, and not merely to embed each finite truncation $I_N$ as a finite set of points, then no fixed finite-dimensional architecture can achieve perfect simulation of a CCR target across all levels.
\end{theorem}

\begin{corollary}
No finite-dimensional semigroup can support an exact representation of CCR identity with $\MO = +\infty$.
